                <pb facs="0389" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg379"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.52/405b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-08T14:00:00-04:00">April 8, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>984. Our 979, April 7, midnight. The British Embassy here has now informed us
                    that Alba apparently had no authority for putting forward the proposal outlined
                    in our telegram under reference. If that be the case of course the proposition
                    in our 936, April 4, 8 p.m. still holds.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
